-- title:
--   Adic points in a chart unit locus factor through V
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime number.
--
--   **Base ring and fraction field.** $\mathcal{O}$ is a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`, absolute unramifiedness). $K_0$ is a field of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficient ring.** $\mathrm{Onr}$ is a commutative domain of characteristic zero, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathrm{Onr}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is a group homomorphism such that $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ holds exactly when $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u \in \mathcal{O}^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** $G$ is a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma \le G$ a subgroup; `hcent` provides $z \in \Gamma$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ ($c \in K_0$) and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z) = 2$, and `hodd` provides $w \in \Gamma$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w) = 1$. The subgroup $\Gamma' \le G$ is characterised by `hΓ'`: $x \in \Gamma'$ iff $x \in \Gamma$ and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ is even. The homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ is the projectivisation of $\sigma$ (`hρ`); `hdisc` says each vertex of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) has finite stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$, and `hcocpt` says there is a finite set of vertices meeting every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit.
--
--   **The candidate quotient scheme.** $\mathcal{X}$ is a scheme and $f : \mathcal{X} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ is proper and flat.
--
--   **The uniformisation datum $\Theta$.** For every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\Theta$ assigns to each pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ for $(K_0,\pi)$ an element of `Scheme.nilpPoints f` at $B$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$. It is assumed natural in $B$ (`hΘnat`); invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, in the sense that whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $\sigma\gamma$ and a pair $x, x'$ — that is, the $\mathrm{Onr}$-component of $x'$ is the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$, and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of that of $x$ — one has $\Theta(x') = \Theta(x)$ (`hΘinv`); and with prescribed geometric fibres (`hΘfib`): for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to k$, the map $P \mapsto \Theta(\psi,P)$ is onto the $k$-points of $f$, and $\Theta(\psi,P) = \Theta(\psi,P')$ iff some $\gamma \in \Gamma$ relates $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ by the twisted action. Finally `hΘuniv` asserts that $\Theta$ is initial with these properties: for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and every family $\rho'$ of the same shape into the nilpotent points of $T$ which is natural and $\Gamma$-invariant in the above senses, there is a natural family $u$ from the nilpotent points of $f$ to those of $T$ with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any natural $u'$ with $u' \circ \Theta = \rho'$ agrees with $u$ on all $B$ and all points.
--
--   **Analytic frame.** $C$ is an algebraically closed, complete valued field (value group $\Gamma_0$) which is a $K_0$-algebra; $R$ is a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, $C$ is an $R$-algebra, and the relevant scalar towers over $\mathcal{O}$ hold. $\varpi$ is a pseudo-uniformizer of $K_0$ in $C$, and `hF : IsAdicFrame π ϖ R` requires: $\pi$ irreducible; $R \to C$ injective with image exactly the closed unit ball $\{v(c) \le 1\}$; $R$ $\pi$-adically complete; the elements of $K_0$ of valuation at most $1$ are exactly those of $\mathcal{O}$; the image of $K_0$ closed in $C$; and $\pi$ mapping to $\varpi$ in $C$. Further, $\psi_0 : \mathrm{Onr} \to R$ is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map; `hrk` says that for $v(x) < 1$ and $y \ne 0$ some power $v(x)^n \le v(y)$; `hval` says every nonzero $\varepsilon \in \Gamma_0$ dominates $v(y)$ for some $y \ne 0$; `hex : Omega.IsExhausted ϖ` says every point of the Drinfeld upper half-plane $C \setminus K_0$ lies in one of the affinoids `affinoid ϖ n`; and the ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ ρ` of holomorphic functions is assumed to be a domain.
--
--   **Uniformisation of adic points.** $\Phi$ sends each adic point $x$ (a compatible system of Deligne data over the rings $R/(\pi^{n+1})$) to a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, and `hΦ` has four clauses: (i) for all $x$ and $n$, the reduction of $\Phi(x)$ along $R \to R/(\pi^{n+1})$ is the morphism $\Theta(\psi_0 \bmod \pi^{n+1},\, x.\mathrm{pt}\,n)$; (ii) $\Phi$ is surjective; (iii) $\Phi(x) = \Phi(x')$ iff $x' = x \cdot \sigma\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma'$; (iv) base change along $R \to C$ is injective on $R$-points of $f$ and every $C$-point of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ comes from an $R$-point.
--
--   **Chart morphisms.** $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`), and $s_n : \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi^{n+1})\bigr) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ is the structure morphism (`hsn`). Writing $A$ for the edge chart ring `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` — the localisation away from `edgeQuot.discr` of the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $\mathrm{Onr}$ by the edge relation, with distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η` — and $A_n = A/(\pi^{n+1})$, the family $\kappa$ assigns to each $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and each $n$ a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A_n \to \mathcal{X} \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}} \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi^{n+1}))$. The hypothesis `hκ` states the chart identity: for all $h$, $n$, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and $\mathrm{Onr}$-algebra $B$ (compatibly) with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\mathrm{Onr}$-algebra map $\bar{x} : A_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, P$ over $B$, if the line of $d$ at the standard full lattice is spanned by $\bar{x}(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, the line of $d$ at $g_1 \cdot (\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under `actBaseChange B g₁` of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar{x}(\eta) \otimes e_1$, and $d$ satisfies `DeligneDatum.InEdgeChart` for the pair $\bigl(g_1\cdot\mathrm{std},\ \mathrm{std}\bigr)$ (at every prime of $B$ the edge nondegeneracy conditions hold), and if $P$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$ (for every full lattice $M$, the line of $P$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $d$ at $h^{-1}M$), then the morphism underlying $\Theta\bigl(\mathrm{Onr} \to B,\ P\bigr)$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\bar{x})$ followed by $\kappa\,h\,n$ followed by the first projection of the pullback.
--
--   **The open set and the chart unit locus.** $V$ is an open subscheme of $\mathcal{X}$, $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, and $t \in A$ is an element whose basic open set at each level lies over $V$: for every $n$, $D\bigl(t \bmod \pi^{n+1}\bigr) \subseteq (\kappa\,h\,n)^{-1}\bigl(\mathrm{pr}_1^{-1}(V)\bigr)$ (`ht`). Finally $S \subseteq C$ is the set characterised by `hS`: $z \in S$ iff $z$ lies in the Drinfeld upper half-plane $C \setminus K_0$ and, for every adic point $x$ with $x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C = z$ and every $n$, there exist a ring homomorphism $\bar{x} : A_n \to R/(\pi^{n+1})$ and a Deligne datum $d$ over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ such that $\bar{x}$ restricted along $\mathrm{Onr} \to A_n$ is $\psi_0$ reduced mod $\pi^{n+1}$; the lines of $d$ at the standard lattice and at $g_1 \cdot (\text{standard lattice})$ are given by $\bar{x}(\xi)$ and $\bar{x}(\eta)$ exactly as in `hκ`, and $d$ lies in the edge chart for $\bigl(g_1\cdot\mathrm{std},\ \mathrm{std}\bigr)$; the level-$n$ datum $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$; and $\bar{x}(t \bmod \pi^{n+1})$ is a unit.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every adic point $x$ of $\mathrm{AdicPoint}\,K_0\,\pi\,R$ and every $z \in C$ with $z = x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and $z \in S$, the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is contained in the preimage of $V$ under the morphism underlying $\Phi(x)$; that is, $\top \le (\Phi x)^{-1}(V)$ as open subsets of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, so $\Phi(x)$ factors through the open subscheme $V$.
--
--   This is a localisation step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: it converts the chart-level containment $D(\bar t) \subseteq \kappa_{h,n}^{-1}(\mathrm{pr}_1^{-1}V)$ into the statement that the $R$-point $\Phi(x)$ attached to an adic point whose upper half-plane coordinate lies in the unit locus $S$ of $t$ lands entirely inside the open $V$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where such pieces are assembled into a cover by loci on which the coordinate function is holomorphic.
